  "articleBody": "Optimizing your website for AI search can feel like navigating new territory. There are some common traps businesses fall into that can actually hinder, rather than help, their visibility in AI Overviews and answer engines. Knowing what to watch out for can save you time and ensure your efforts are truly impactful.\n\nWhat to Do Next:\n\n*   **Don't Rely Solely on Image-Based Content:** AI systems struggle to interpret text embedded in images. Make sure all your important information, especially answers to common questions, is available as visible, crawlable text.\n*   **Avoid Marking Up Invisible Content:** Structured data is powerful, but it must accurately reflect what users can see on the page. Adding schema for content that isn't visible can be misleading and may even be considered spammy by search engines.\n*   **Don't Treat Structured Data as a Magic Bullet:** While crucial, structured data isn't a guarantee of ranking or AI citation. It's a tool to help AI understand your content better. The content itself still needs to be high quality, useful, and accurate.\n*   **Be Careful with Indexing Controls:** Accidentally blocking valuable pages with `noindex` tags or other preview controls can prevent AI crawlers from accessing your content. Regularly review your robots.txt and meta tags.\n*   **Don't Overlook Core Accessibility:** Neglecting accessibility basics like keyboard navigation, text alternatives for non-text content, contrast ratios, and logical page structure isn't just bad for users; it can also make your site less machine-readable and understandable for AI.\n*   **Don't Assume \"More Content\" is Always Better:** Simply generating vast amounts of generic, low-quality AI content can backfire. Focus on fact density, clarity, and semantic relevance, ensuring every piece provides genuine value.\n\nIf your website relies heavily on complex JavaScript, has intricate template structures, or you're unsure about your accessibility compliance, bringing in a technical SEO or web performance specialist can be incredibly beneficial. They can help you identify and fix these kinds of issues effectively.",
  "datePublished": "2026-09-23"
